WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.590
Welcome to Planning. In this lesson, we explore this purpose: Make feasible work commitments supported by scope, resources and risks.

2
00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:19.620
Consider this scenario. A schedule assumes team members are available when they are not. First understand the problem before producing documentation.

3
00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:29.620
Start with two steps: Define scope and deliverables. Then Estimate work and resources. Each step should be explained and evidenced.

4
00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:39.420
Continue with Negotiate achievable commitments. Then Maintain the plan as facts change. Verify the results against the intended outcome.

5
00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:59.770
Stronger evidence looks like this: Stronger: contemporaneous integrated plan, dependency map, commitment record tied to real work. Weaker evidence would be: Weaker: creating a fixed timeline without capacity assumptions; no trace of consistent use. Triangulate independent sources.

6
00:00:59.770 --> 00:01:14.020
Now your turn. Review four documents and two interviews, identify inconsistencies and complete the mastery challenge. This video is an independent teaching explanation, not official CMMI model wording.
